@host = https://localhost:7126
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..Ene5Gzf9RFg2qhh3awnJJOtimgHQ8D5tbv7tD1Plm7I
@branchId = ba7c4374-a68b-4c60-ab06-55ac62505670
@productId = ca6f2e9a-24b5-4194-bb2a-66ce34b6a469
@sourceLocationId = 46599a6f-bc0f-4cf8-b6ad-83e9312a042c
@destinationLocationId = c2727378-b800-4077-b7cf-4541a97af1b1
@transferId = 6757e1cd-42ac-4edd-8a26-410ac776d3db
@expectedRevision = 2

# Use active references, with at least 5 units in the central source location.
# destinationLocationId must belong to branchId.
# Before EACH price PUT, set expectedRevision from the current GET response.
# Use 0 only when no price record exists (404).

### 1. Read existing pricing and copy revision to expectedRevision
GET {{host}}/api/branches/{{branchId}}/product-prices/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Set initial baseline to 100
PUT {{host}}/api/branches/{{branchId}}/product-prices/{{productId}}/baseline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 100,
  "expectedRevision": {{expectedRevision}},
  "reason": "Transfer receipt pricing test: initial baseline"
}

### 3. Create a NEW transfer after applying the migration; copy its id to transferId
POST {{host}}/api/stock-transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceLocationId": "{{sourceLocationId}}",
  "destinationLocationId": "{{destinationLocationId}}",
  "notes": "Keep newer baseline on receipt",
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 5,
      "baselineUnitPrice": 100
    }
  ]
}

### 4. Ship
POST {{host}}/api/stock-transfers/{{transferId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Set newer baseline to 150 (refresh expectedRevision first)
PUT {{host}}/api/branches/{{branchId}}/product-prices/{{productId}}/baseline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 150,
  "expectedRevision": {{expectedRevision}},
  "reason": "Inflation adjustment while transfer is in transit"
}

### 6. Record destination quantity before receipt
GET {{host}}/api/stock/balances?inventoryLocationId={{destinationLocationId}}&productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Receive: 200, status Received; transfer line still has baseline 100
POST {{host}}/api/stock-transfers/{{transferId}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Must still be 150; minimumSellingPrice must be unchanged
GET {{host}}/api/branches/{{branchId}}/product-prices/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Destination quantity must have increased by exactly 5
GET {{host}}/api/stock/balances?inventoryLocationId={{destinationLocationId}}&productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Repeat receipt: 200, no extra stock or price history
POST {{host}}/api/stock-transfers/{{transferId}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. The manual change to 150 remains; no TransferReceipt price change for this transfer
GET {{host}}/api/branches/{{branchId}}/product-prices/{{productId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Additional scenarios are described in docs/transfer-receipt-pricing.md.



